<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Sitemap for REV Grant Administration.

  The grouping is not cosmetic - it separates the three things the process owner does:

    Casework      the day-to-day queues. "Applications" opens on the Active Applications view,
                  which excludes Auto-reject (rev_status ne 4) - that is FR-020 implemented as a
                  view filter rather than as data movement, so nothing is hidden irreversibly.
                  "Borderline - Awaiting Review" is the FR-019 queue and is given its own entry
                  rather than being buried as a view, because 100% of Borderline outcomes must
                  reach a human (NFR-018) and a queue nobody clicks is not a control.
                  "Auto-rejected Applications" is the separate rejected list FR-020 asks for.
                  "Under Review - Incomplete Scoring" is the FR-022 queue: applications where a
                  scored answer was missing, so no automated outcome was issued at all.

    Configuration the rev_setting rows. This is what FR-017 and NFR-019 buy - the board changes
                  the knockout threshold, the borderline band and the income ceiling here,
                  with no flow edit, no solution import and no developer. Auditing is enabled on
                  this table, so every change is evidence against the decisions it affected.

    Operations    the error log. FR-010 requires a failure to be visible rather than silent;
                  this is where it becomes visible. Unresolved Errors is the default view.

  Applicants sits under Casework rather than being the app's front door: ADR-013 makes the
  applicant's primary name column a pseudonymised reference, so an applicant list is a list of
  codes. The application is the useful entry point, and the applicant is reached through it.

  LOCATION IS FIXED BY THE PACKER, NOT BY CONVENTION.
  This is an APP sitemap (ComponentType.AppModuleSiteMap, 81), not the organisation sitemap
  (ComponentType.SiteMap, 62), and the two have different homes. SolutionPackagerLib maps
  AppModuleSiteMap to directory "AppModuleSiteMaps", file "$(PrimaryName)/AppModuleSiteMap.xml",
  so it lives in its own top-level folder rather than beside AppModule.xml.

  EVERY ELEMENT BELOW IS GROUND TRUTH, NOT A GUESS - REWRITTEN COMPLETE 2026-08-14.
  This file went through three wrong hand-authored shapes before this one, each caught by a
  live `pac solution import` against DEV and each looking equally plausible beforehand. Rather
  than guess a fourth time, the fix was to create a real, working sitemap directly via the Web
  API (POST to /sitemaps, isappaware=true - the sitemap entity is NOT on Microsoft's
  create-via-solution-import-unsupported list, unlike Entities/OptionSets/Roles/
  FieldSecurityProfiles - see ensure-schema.ps1's header), then `pac solution export` +
  `pac solution unpack` it to see exactly how Dataverse itself serialises the result. Every
  wrong assumption below is kept in this comment rather than deleted, because the same
  plausible-but-fabricated shapes are exactly the ones a future edit would reintroduce:

    - WRONG: <SiteMapName>. There is no such element. The display name comes through
      <LocalizedNames><LocalizedName description="..." languagecode="1033" /></LocalizedNames>,
      exactly like AppModule.xml's own <LocalizedNames> one folder over - a pattern this file
      should have followed from the start instead of inventing a sibling to <SiteMapUniqueName>.
    - WRONG: <sitemapid>. Not part of this file at all. Dataverse assigns the sitemapid itself
      on creation, the same as it does for Role and FieldSecurityProfile ids (see Roles/*.xml
      and FieldSecurityProfiles.xml for that same pattern) - a fixed GUID declared here would
      only ever have been the value AppModule.xml's type="62" AppModuleComponent needs to
      reference, and that value can only be known AFTER this component is created for real.
    - WRONG: <IsCustomizable>, <IntroducedVersion> as direct children of <AppModuleSiteMap>.
      Neither appears in a real export. IntroducedVersion DOES appear, but as an ATTRIBUTE on
      the nested <SiteMap> element below, not as a sibling of SiteMapUniqueName.
    - WRONG: <SiteMapXml> as a wrapper, with the sitemap markup serialised as a CDATA string
      inside it. There is no <SiteMapXml> element. The real element is <SiteMap> itself,
      appearing as a DIRECT CHILD of <AppModuleSiteMap> with literal nested XML - Area/Group/
      SubArea/Titles/Title as real child elements, not text. (The CDATA attempt was itself a
      correction of an earlier, equally wrong assumption that <SiteMapXml> read as literal XML;
      it was the wrapper element's name that was fabricated all along, not the encoding inside
      it.) Because this content is literal child XML again, not text, the &amp;-escaping on the
      three SubArea Url attributes below is correct XML and stays exactly as originally written.
    - CORRECT, kept unchanged: <SiteMapUniqueName> as a child element populated with the schema
      name - the one guess in the original file that a live import never once complained about.

  Also newly added, because the real export always includes them: <EnableCollapsibleGroups>,
  <ShowHome>, <ShowPinned>, <ShowRecents> - the same four booleans documented on the sitemap
  Web API entity itself, defaulted here to the values Dataverse itself defaults a new sitemap to.

  THIS ALSO CHANGES OTHER/SOLUTION.XML AND APPMODULE.XML, NOT YET DONE HERE.
  AppModule.xml's <AppModuleComponent type="62" id="{d4f6a8b0-4002-...}" /> reference still
  points at the fabricated GUID this file used to declare via <sitemapid>. That reference
  cannot be corrected until this sitemap has been created for real by a successful import and
  its live sitemapid read back - exactly the same live-id reconciliation already done once for
  Roles/*.xml and FieldSecurityProfiles.xml. Left as the next diagnosed failure rather than
  guessed at here, per this file's own now-proven point about guessing this component's shape.
-->
<AppModuleSiteMap xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <SiteMapUniqueName>rev_grantadministration</SiteMapUniqueName>
  <EnableCollapsibleGroups>False</EnableCollapsibleGroups>
  <ShowHome>True</ShowHome>
  <ShowPinned>True</ShowPinned>
  <ShowRecents>True</ShowRecents>
  <SiteMap IntroducedVersion="1.0.0.0">
    <Area Id="rev_area_grantadmin" ShowGroups="true" Title="Grant Administration" Description="Grant application administration">
      <Titles>
        <Title LCID="1033" Title="Grant Administration" />
      </Titles>

      <!--
      GROUND TRUTH, 2026-08-19 — THE VIEW-PINNED SUB-AREA SHAPE CAME FROM THE PLATFORM
      The five sub-areas that must open a SPECIFIC view carried BOTH Entity= and
      Url="?pagetype=..." and every one of them opened the table's DEFAULT view instead. The
      reviewer had reasonably concluded that pinning a view to a sub-area was a platform
      limitation.

      Rather than guess a second time — the first guess is what produced the broken shape — the
      reviewer changed them in the SITE MAP DESIGNER and published, and the platform's own
      serialisation was then read back through the Web API. It differs in three ways, and this
      file now matches it exactly:

        - NO Entity= attribute at all. A sub-area is EITHER an entity sub-area OR a URL one.
        - the Url begins with `&`, not `?`
        - `&viewType=1039` is appended — 1039 is the savedquery type code, which tells the
          client the viewid names a system view rather than a personal one

      The designer also writes ResourceId="SitemapDesigner.NewSubArea" and a transparent-spacer
      Icon on sub-areas it creates. Both are designer defaults with real Titles supplied here
      already, so they are deliberately NOT copied — the two things copied are the two that
      carry meaning.

      ⚠ REVISED AGAIN 2026-08-19, THIRD SHAPE — AND THIS TIME FROM MICROSOFT'S OWN SITEMAP.
      The `&pagetype=...` fragment above was wrong too, and worse than the original: with the
      app-membership defect fixed, the sub-pages did not fall back to the default view, they
      DISAPPEARED from play mode entirely, and the app designer rejected the value saying it
      expects a web resource. That error is the platform telling us what `Url` means: it is a
      URL, not a set of parameters to append.

      GROUND TRUTH, from a Microsoft-authored MANAGED sitemap in this same environment —
      the `Power Platform Environment Settings` app, 25 of whose sub-areas carry a Url:

        Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=control&amp;controlName=PowerAdmin...&amp;data={...}"
        Url="/tools/externappmanagement/externappmanagement.aspx"

      So the shape is a ROOT-RELATIVE path — a leading `/`, then `?`, then the query string.
      That also answers the solution-awareness objection, which was the right objection: a
      leading-slash URL carries NO host and no environment-specific value, so it is identical
      in dev, tst_acc and prd and cannot breach C-TECH-047. The viewid is a solution component
      id, hand-authored in SavedQueries/ precisely so it is stable across environments.

      ONE THING IS STILL NOT GROUND-TRUTHED: whether `viewid` wants braces. Microsoft's own
      examples here carry no viewid to copy, and the site map designer wrote it bare. So this
      file deliberately ships THREE VARIANTS across the Application sub-pages, to settle it in
      one deploy instead of three:

        rev_sub_borderline          viewid=%7bGUID%7d   (encoded braces)
        rev_sub_incompletescoring   viewid=GUID         (bare, as the designer wrote it)
        rev_sub_autorejected        viewid={GUID}       (literal braces)

      The two Grant sub-areas use the encoded form. THIS IS A DIAGNOSTIC STATE AND MUST NOT
      SURVIVE: whichever variant renders, all five adopt it and this comment shrinks to the
      answer. See IMP-0087.
      -->
      <Group Id="rev_group_casework" Title="Casework" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Casework" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_applications" Entity="rev_application" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" DefaultDashboard="">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Applications" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_borderline" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_application&amp;viewid=%7be5a7b9c1-6003-4a2b-8c11-0a1b2c3d4e53%7d">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Borderline - Awaiting Review" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_incompletescoring" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_application&amp;viewid=e5a7b9c1-6004-4a2b-8c11-0a1b2c3d4e54">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Under Review - Incomplete Scoring" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_autorejected" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_application&amp;viewid={e5a7b9c1-6005-4a2b-8c11-0a1b2c3d4e55}">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Auto-rejected Applications" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_applicants" Entity="rev_applicant" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Applicants" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

      <!--
        GRANTS - ADDED 2026-08-19. rev_grant shipped in WBS 0.4 with an Entity.xml, a main form
        and three saved queries, and NO SubArea anywhere in this file, so none of it was
        reachable from the app's navigation. The reviewer confirmed on 2026-08-19 that the
        grant table and its views/forms should have been available in the model-driven app.

        WHY NOTHING CAUGHT IT: `verify-forms-and-views-reachable.py` asserts that FormXml/ and
        SavedQueries/ content is reachable from Entity.xml at PACK time - that the packer will
        not silently drop it. Whether a HUMAN can navigate to it is a different question, about
        this file, and nothing asked it until `verify-shipped-content.py` was written.

        The three view ids below are read from the saved-query files themselves, not invented:
          AllGrants           {e1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a1}  (isdefault=1)
          AwaitingAcceptance  {e1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2}
          AcceptanceSigned    {e1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a3}
        The default view needs no Url - the entity SubArea opens it. The two working lists
        carry an explicit viewid, exactly as the rev_application working lists above do.
      -->
      <Group Id="rev_group_grants" Title="Grants" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Grants" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_grants" Entity="rev_grant" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" DefaultDashboard="">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Grants" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_awaitingacceptance" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_grant&amp;viewid=%7be1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2%7d">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Awaiting Acceptance" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_acceptancesigned" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_grant&amp;viewid=%7be1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a3%7d">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Acceptance Signed" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

      <!--
        REVIEWS - ADDED FOR WBS 6.4. Same lesson as the Grants group above (IMP-0052/IMP-0060/
        IMP-0090): an entity with a Entity.xml, a main form and saved queries is NOT reachable
        until it also has a SubArea here AND an AppModuleComponent in AppModule.xml (both done
        in this change) AND the audit switch in the environment (cannot be done from this
        session - recorded as a Dev Summary post-deploy item).

        The default SubArea uses the plain Entity= form with no Url at all, proven working on
        every other default-view SubArea in this file (rev_sub_applications, rev_sub_grants).
        The filtered SubArea adopts the SAME encoded-braces viewid form the two Grant working
        lists above use (%7bGUID%7d) - deliberately NOT a fourth guess at the still-unresolved
        viewid-encoding question the comment above this Group documents (IMP-0087/IMP-0091):
        "whichever variant renders, all five adopt it" - Grants already chose encoded braces,
        so Reviews follows that choice rather than adding a new one. The view id is read from
        Entities/rev_review/SavedQueries/AwaitingFinalisation.xml, not invented.
      -->
      <Group Id="rev_group_reviews" Title="Reviews" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Reviews" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_reviews" Entity="rev_review" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" DefaultDashboard="">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Reviews" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_awaitingfinalisation" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_review&amp;viewid=%7be3000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2%7d">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Awaiting Finalisation" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

      <!--
        FINANCE - ADDED 2026-08-26, WBS 6.1/6.9 DEFECT FIX. rev_roundfinance shipped with an
        Entity.xml and REV Admin already holding Create/Read/Write privileges
        (Roles/REV Admin/REV Admin.xml:154-163, interim maintainer pending the REV Finance
        role — TAD ADR-028 section 6.1, A-R25) but no SubArea here and no form/view content
        at all. The reviewer confirmed live that the table could not be managed through this
        app despite the privilege grant - the exact IMP-0090 pattern (privilege granted,
        navigation surface never added), this time with the form/view content itself also
        missing rather than merely unreachable.

        Default SubArea (no Url) opens AllRoundFinances.xml, this table's own isdefault="1"
        view - same plain Entity= shape already proven on rev_sub_applications/rev_sub_grants/
        rev_sub_reviews above. The filtered SubArea adopts the SAME encoded-braces viewid form
        (%7bGUID%7d) the Grants/Reviews groups above already settled on (IMP-0087/IMP-0091):
        "whichever variant renders, all five adopt it" - now six. The view id is read from
        Entities/rev_roundfinance/SavedQueries/ActiveRoundFinances.xml, not invented.
      -->
      <Group Id="rev_group_finance" Title="Finance" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Finance" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_roundfinance" Entity="rev_roundfinance" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" DefaultDashboard="">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Round Finance" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_activeroundfinances" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All" Url="/main.aspx?pagetype=entitylist&amp;etn=rev_roundfinance&amp;viewid=%7bfece6e75-d33a-43ae-8f83-7848838c2ceb%7d">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Active Round Finances" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

      <Group Id="rev_group_configuration" Title="Configuration" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Configuration" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_settings" Entity="rev_setting" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Scoring Settings" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

      <Group Id="rev_group_operations" Title="Operations" IsProfile="false">
        <Titles>
          <Title LCID="1033" Title="Operations" />
        </Titles>
        <SubArea Id="rev_sub_errorlog" Entity="rev_errorlog" Client="All" AvailableOffline="false" PassParams="false" Sku="All">
          <Titles>
            <Title LCID="1033" Title="Error Log" />
          </Titles>
        </SubArea>
      </Group>

    </Area>
  </SiteMap>
  <LocalizedNames>
    <LocalizedName description="REV Grant Administration" languagecode="1033" />
  </LocalizedNames>
</AppModuleSiteMap>
